# 110blackmagic_arm_adi_merged.patch
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# ---------------------
# Consolidates ARM ADIv5/v6 DAP, SWD caching, Cortex-M, and flashstub optimizations
# (formerly patches 12, 33, 42, 57, 88, 90, and ARM portions of 82bis, 83bis, 105):
#
# 1. ARM ADIv5 / ADIv6 register caching (formerly patches 83bis, 88, 90):
#    Standard Blackmagic issues DP-SELECT and AP-CSW writes on every single memory access or
#    register setup. In hot memory read/write loops, repeating identical DP-SELECT and AP-CSW
#    transfers wastes substantial SWD bandwidth. Caching the last written DP-SELECT, DP-SELECT1
#    (ADIv6 upper AP address bits), and AP-CSW allows skipping redundant writes so warm transfers
#    only need to send TAR and data.
#    Furthermore, when the target undergoes an SWD line reset, power cycle, or nRST, hardware
#    registers revert to default while the software cache thought they were still valid;
#    therefore, caches must be properly partitioned into DP-level (SELECT/SELECT1) and AP-level
#    (CSW) invalidation and flushed on reset events.
#
# 2. Direct SWD fast path (formerly patch 33):
#    Redirects adiv5_xx_no_check directly to swindle's native ln_adiv5xxx_no_check SWD routines,
#    bypassing unnecessary abstraction layers.
#
# 3. Cortex-M33 / ARMv8-M stack limit registers (formerly patch 42):
#    Exposes psplim and msplim registers in cortex.h and cortexm.c for ARMv8-M / Cortex-M33
#    targets to support hardware stack overflow protection debugging.
#
# 4. Flashstub interrupt disabling (formerly patch 57):
#    When executing RAM flashstubs to write flash (e.g. on RP2040), target interrupts can fire
#    and derail execution, causing flash programming to fail.
#
# 5. Architecture tagging & unused code reduction (formerly patches 12, 82bis, 105):
#    - Disables unused Cortex-R target support to save firmware flash.
#    - Tags ARM architecture on target via TOPT_ARCH_ARM.
#    - Disables obsolete C XML target descriptions in cortexm.c because target.xml is generated
#      by zero-heap Rust code.
#
# FIX
# ---
# 1. In adiv5.c, adiv5.h, adiv5_internal.h, adi.c, and adiv6.c:
#    - Add select_cache, select1_cache, and csw_cache with validity flags.
#    - In adiv5_ap_select(), adiv6_ap_reg_write(), and adi_ap_mem_access_setup(), skip writes
#      when values match the cache.
#    - Provide adiv5_dp_invalidate_caches() (called on line reset) and adiv5_ap_invalidate_caches()
#      (called on target reset) to flush cached state when the target reverts to reset defaults.
#
# 2. In adiv5_swd.c, wire adiv5_dp_write_no_check and adiv5_ap_write_no_check to ln_adiv5xxx.
#
# 3. In cortex.h and cortexm.c, add CORTEXM_REG_MSPLIM and CORTEXM_REG_PSPLIM register mappings.
#
# 4. In cortexm.c cortexm_run_stub(), disable interrupts during flashstub execution.
#
# 5. In cortexm.c, disable legacy C target description XML generators (#if 0) and update
#    target_is_cortexm() to check target->attach.
#
